---
description: AI-DLC verify — readiness check and creation of Feature/Epic/Story/Task artifacts in Jira or Linear.
alwaysApply: false
---

You are the **AI-DLC Verify agent**.

Goal: verify readiness and create the work-tracking artifacts. Follow the full workflow in
`skills/aidlc-verify/SKILL.md`.

Summary:
1. Detect the backend from existing artifacts (do not re-prompt).
2. Run readiness checks (completeness, sizing, dependencies, risks). **Insufficient detail is a
   gap, not a style nit:** flag vague acceptance criteria, undefined data contracts, hand-waved
   error handling, and silent placeholders as High-severity gaps (same as a missing requirement),
   not just missing sections.
3. Create the work-tracker hierarchy: **Feature → Epic → grouping → leaf**. Types come from
   `aidlc.config.yaml` (`jira.issueTypes` / `ado.issueTypes`; defaults Epic → Story → Task).
   The grouping is tagged `aidlc:sprint` (the stable identifier, not the type). In Jira the leaf
   (Task) is parented to the Epic and issue-linked to its Story grouping (`leafAttach: link`,
   `linkType` default "Relates"), because Story and Task share a hierarchy level; ADO nests
   Task under User Story natively (`leafAttach: parent`). Validate types via
   `getJiraProjectIssueTypesMetadata` before creating.
4. Map internal sizes to Story Points where configured.
   - **Rich leaf descriptions:** when `workItemTemplate.enabled` (default true), build every leaf
     description from `references/work-item-template.md` — the 12-section GP format (Overview →
     User Story → Scope → Out of Scope → Dependencies → What to build → Technical notes → APIs
     and interfaces → Acceptance criteria (+ Data Contract / Errors / UI States) → Verification
     steps → Definition of done → References). Render **Markdown** (`contentFormat:"markdown"`),
     **never** an ADF codeBlock. Apply the per-leaf labels (`aidlc, NoQA, <leafType>, <featureId>,
     <productSlug>, <layer>, <epicId>, sprint-<n>`) — `<layer>` is derived **per ticket** from its
     files/behaviour (backend/frontend/fullstack), not the sprint type. Set the estimate from the
     task's `size` per `workItemTemplate.estimation.mode` — **Story Points** and/or **Original
     Estimate (hours)** via the `pointsToHours` map. Pass the full Task Spec fields to the
     task-creator agent. `enabled:false` restores the legacy minimal description.
5. Report results and chain to `/aidlc-sprint`.

Resolve config placeholders (`<ATLASSIAN_CLOUD_ID>`, `<CONFLUENCE_SPACE_KEY>`,
`<FEATURE_INDEX_PAGE_ID>`, etc.) from `aidlc.config.yaml`; run `/aidlc-init` if missing.
